peratorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-5+\\frac{4}{\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5+\\frac{4}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-5\\theta +4}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ -5\\theta +4 & =0 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{4}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" "answer-7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" "answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" "answer-dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" "answer-7bb1b0f3-0b13-5864-83a1-105f6280eef0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" :answer/id #uuid "7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" :answer/id #uuid "7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer/id #uuid "44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" :answer/id #uuid "dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bb1b0f3-0b13-5864-83a1-105f6280eef0" :answer/id #uuid "7bb1b0f3-0b13-5864-83a1-105f6280eef0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257" :question/id #uuid "953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257" :question/math-academy-id "q-159970" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Poisson random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-4\\theta +8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡24\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-4\\theta +8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡24) \\\\  & =-4+\\frac{8}{\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+\\frac{8}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-4\\theta +8}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ -4\\theta +8 & =0 \\\\ \\theta  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/id #uuid "332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" "answer-05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591" "answer-fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5" "answer-f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1" "answer-7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" :answer/id #uuid "4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591" :answer/id #uuid "05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5" :answer/id #uuid "fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1" :answer/id #uuid "f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8" :answer/id #uuid "7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" :question/id #uuid "d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" :question/math-academy-id "q-159942" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent normal random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-3.54+2.2\\text{ }\\,\\theta -3\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-3.54+2.2\\text{ }\\,\\theta -3\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =2.2-6\\text{ }\\,\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.2-6\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 6\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =2.2 \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.367\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.367,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5a1816a3-cd64-5456-9517-95ae4181b629"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5a1816a3-cd64-5456-9517-95ae4181b629" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1816a3-cd64-5456-9517-95ae4181b629" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-12790bd2-fdb6-5ae2-9339-61f0fb556461" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c15cc0bb-88d7-5a65-b0be-5fe61a791505" "answer-e0b77137-f026-54f7-b0e8-585ac5b704af" "answer-56d327c3-e05f-5754-88f5-dbc857c6043f" "answer-12790bd2-fdb6-5ae2-9339-61f0fb556461" "answer-1127dce4-9c1c-5edb-917f-38707912afec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c15cc0bb-88d7-5a65-b0be-5fe61a791505" :answer/id #uuid "c15cc0bb-88d7-5a65-b0be-5fe61a791505" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.065" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0b77137-f026-54f7-b0e8-585ac5b704af" :answer/id #uuid "e0b77137-f026-54f7-b0e8-585ac5b704af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.112" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56d327c3-e05f-5754-88f5-dbc857c6043f" :answer/id #uuid "56d327c3-e05f-5754-88f5-dbc857c6043f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.204" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12790bd2-fdb6-5ae2-9339-61f0fb556461" :answer/id #uuid "12790bd2-fdb6-5ae2-9339-61f0fb556461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.367" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1127dce4-9c1c-5edb-917f-38707912afec" :answer/id #uuid "1127dce4-9c1c-5edb-917f-38707912afec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.073" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d69af2de-f48e-5047-98b1-6977b8b554d5" :question/id #uuid "d69af2de-f48e-5047-98b1-6977b8b554d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-159940" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent exponential random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -7.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -7.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\theta }-7.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\theta }-7.8 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\theta } & =7.8 \\\\ 4 & =7.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta  \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.513\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.513,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0558f9a-6e48-5095-9d94-0109cf7402ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0558f9a-6e48-5095-9d94-0109cf7402ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0558f9a-6e48-5095-9d94-0109cf7402ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f91e9e3e-0341-5556-a0b5-5691bcc58340" :answer-field/choices ["an