-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-22e80040-d18e-5faa-af39-593a97881279" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d8bb5ed-e27a-5e79-a56d-335ca515db9c" "answer-22e80040-d18e-5faa-af39-593a97881279" "answer-6f07d653-9ff4-5a87-a55f-d3592fa58cf3" "answer-d50a9899-221a-5f45-912c-5d49f82f44f6" "answer-18079953-7a0d-57a4-8843-c654a6bb39fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d8bb5ed-e27a-5e79-a56d-335ca515db9c" :answer/id #uuid "4d8bb5ed-e27a-5e79-a56d-335ca515db9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.581" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22e80040-d18e-5faa-af39-593a97881279" :answer/id #uuid "22e80040-d18e-5faa-af39-593a97881279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.617" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f07d653-9ff4-5a87-a55f-d3592fa58cf3" :answer/id #uuid "6f07d653-9ff4-5a87-a55f-d3592fa58cf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.714" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d50a9899-221a-5f45-912c-5d49f82f44f6" :answer/id #uuid "d50a9899-221a-5f45-912c-5d49f82f44f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.819" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18079953-7a0d-57a4-8843-c654a6bb39fe" :answer/id #uuid "18079953-7a0d-57a4-8843-c654a6bb39fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.891" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4510ff72-383e-5b2d-aa54-f6d78aa69e2d" :question/id #uuid "4510ff72-383e-5b2d-aa54-f6d78aa69e2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-159939" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent exponential random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -15.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -15.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\theta }-15.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\theta }-15.8 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\theta } & =15.8 \\\\ 5 & =15.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta  \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.316\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.316,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34a1e506-0c01-548c-8aeb-dbb4e0856d79"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34a1e506-0c01-548c-8aeb-dbb4e0856d79" :answer-field/id #uuid "34a1e506-0c01-548c-8aeb-dbb4e0856d79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf461d27-016b-5aa4-a77d-15596b89f756" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5562092f-3fe0-5bcf-8339-c7daec6026f2" "answer-56b4bf5e-9806-5a09-a3b3-65589f4e73ef" "answer-8bedb81d-563d-5133-aea2-1add3162bcde" "answer-cf461d27-016b-5aa4-a77d-15596b89f756" "answer-aa8e2520-683e-5f18-9745-b1b59e87e0a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5562092f-3fe0-5bcf-8339-c7daec6026f2" :answer/id #uuid "5562092f-3fe0-5bcf-8339-c7daec6026f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.208" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56b4bf5e-9806-5a09-a3b3-65589f4e73ef" :answer/id #uuid "56b4bf5e-9806-5a09-a3b3-65589f4e73ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.213" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bedb81d-563d-5133-aea2-1add3162bcde" :answer/id #uuid "8bedb81d-563d-5133-aea2-1add3162bcde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.276" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf461d27-016b-5aa4-a77d-15596b89f756" :answer/id #uuid "cf461d27-016b-5aa4-a77d-15596b89f756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.316" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa8e2520-683e-5f18-9745-b1b59e87e0a4" :answer/id #uuid "aa8e2520-683e-5f18-9745-b1b59e87e0a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.412" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163265 :tutorial/content "Suppose we have a random sample $X_1, X_2, X_3$ drawn from a population where $X_i\\sim B(5,\\theta),$ where $\\theta$ is an unknown probability of success. Let's assume we conducted our sample and got the following data:\n\n$$\nx_1 = 4, \\qquad x_2 = 1, \\qquad x_3 = 1\n$$\n\nIt can be shown that the log-likelihood function for this sample is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = \\ln  125 + 6 \\ln \\theta +9\\ln(1-\\theta).\n$$\n\nOur goal is to form an estimate for the unknown parameter $\\theta.$ To do this, we find the value of $\\theta$ that maximizes the probability of getting the observed sample data. In other words, we need to maximize the likelihood function $L(\\theta).$ And, since the natural logarithm is an increasing function, a value of $\\theta$ that maximizes the likelihood function $L(\\theta)$ will also maximize the log-likelihood function $l(\\theta).$\n\nEstimates of an unknown parameter $\\theta$ obtained by maximizing the likelihood function (or, equivalently, the log-likelihood function) are called **maximum likelihood estimates**. We'll use the usual $\\hat{\\theta}$ notation to denote a maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta.$ \n\n![](images/00/005367bc78937c5bd5b684cb260aff951de2e85d7c2907bb6e11c312ad4f24bd.png)\n\nTo find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡125+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{9}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{9}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{9}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{6(\\theta -1)+9\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 6(\\theta -1)+9\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 15\\theta -6 & =0 \\\\ 15\\theta  & =6 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{6}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} =  \\dfrac{6}{15}.$ \n\n**Note**: It's easy to check that this is a maximum of $l(\\theta)$ by calculating the second derivative. We'll omit this step." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163361 :tutorial/content "Let's derive a general expression for the maximum likelihood estimator for the unknown parameter $\\theta$ for a set of $n$ independent and identically distributed Bernoulli random variables.\n\nSuppose $X_1,X_2,\\ldots,X_{n}$ is an I.I.D random sample, where $X_i\\sim \\text{Bernoulli}(\\theta)$ with unknown probability of success $\\theta.$ For a particular sample $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n},$ the log-likelihood function is given by\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = S\\ln\\theta + (n-S)\\ln(1-\\theta),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\displaystyle S = \\sum_ {i=1}^n x_i$ is the number of successes in the sample. \n\nTo compute a general expression for the maximum likelihood estimate, we differentiate $l(\\theta),$ set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(S\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +(n-S)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{S}{\\theta }+\\frac{n-S}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{S}{\\theta }+\\frac{n-S}{\\theta -1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{S}{\\theta }+\\frac{n-S}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{S(\\theta -1)+(n-S)\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ S(\\theta -1)+(n-S)\\theta  & =0 \\\\ \\cancel{S\\theta }-S+n\\theta -\\cancel{S\\theta } & =0 \\\\ n\\theta -S & =0 \\\\ n\\theta  & =S \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{S}{n} \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is \n\n$$\n\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} =  \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_ {i=1}^n x_i,\n$$\n\nwhich is simply the *mean of the sample*. \n\nThe maximum likelihood estimate for other common distributions can be derived similarly. Let's summarize the most important cases." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163362 :tutorial/content "The table below summarizes the maximum likelihood estimates for several common probability distributions. These results can be derived by maximizing the corresponding log-likelihood function. \n\n| **Distribution** | **Probability Mass Function, $f(x; \\theta)$** | **Parameter, $\\theta$** | **Maximum Likelihood Estimate, $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Bernoulli | $\\displaystyle \\theta^x(1-\\theta)^{1-x}$ | The probability of success | $\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i$ \n The mean of the sample |\n| Binomial | $\\displaystyle {N \\choose x} \\theta^x (1-\\theta)^{N-x}$ | The probability of success | $\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i$ \n The mean of the sample |\n| Poisson | $\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\theta^{x} e^{-\\theta}}{x!}$ | The rate parameter | $\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i$ \n The mean of the sample |\n| Geometric | $\\displaystyle (1-\\theta)^{x-1} \\theta$ | The probability of success | $\\displaystyle \\bigg( \\dfrac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i \\bigg)^{-1}$ \n The reciprocal of the sample mean |\n| Exponential | $\\displaystyle \\theta e^{-\\theta x}$ | The rate parameter | $\\displaystyle \\bigg( \\dfrac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i \\bigg)^{-1}$ \n The reciprocal of the sample mean |\n| Normal | $\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{\\theta_2 \\sqrt{2\\pi}} e^{-\\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{x-\\theta_1}{\\theta_2} \\right)^2}$ | The mean $(\\theta_1)$ \n\n The standard deviation $(\\theta_2)$ | $\\displaystyle \\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}_1 = \\dfrac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i$ \n The mean of the sample \n\n $\\displaystyle \\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}_2 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i-\\overline{x})^2}$ \n The standard deviation of the sample |" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162205 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186161681 :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = 3\\ln\\theta + 4\\ln(1-\\theta),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ from this sample?"] [17592186161681 :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{\\theta -1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3(\\theta -1)+4\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 3(\\theta -1)+4\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 7\\theta -3 & =0 \\\\ 7\\theta  & =3 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} =  \\dfrac{3}{7}.$"] [17592186161682 :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent normal random variables $X_i\\sim N(\\theta,1)$ is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = -6\\ln(2\\pi)-8.4 + 12.1\\, \\! \\theta - 6\\ \\! \\theta^2,\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ for this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."] [17592186161682 :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-8.4+12.1\\,\\,\\theta -6\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =12.1-12\\text{ }\\,\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12.1-12\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 12\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =12.1 \\\\ \\theta  & ≈1.008\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} \\approx 1.008,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places."] [17592186162395 :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?"] [17592186162395 :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\theta }+\\frac{1}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\theta }+\\frac{1}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\theta }+\\frac{1}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5(\\theta -1)+\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 5(\\theta -1)+\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 6\\theta -5 & =0 \\\\ 6\\theta  & =5 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{5}{6}.$"] [17592186162395 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186159572 :answer-field/correct 17592186159574] ["question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/id #uuid "8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c"] ["question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/math-academy-id "q-159963"] ["question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?"] ["question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8(\\theta -1)+12\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 8(\\theta -1)+12\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 20\\theta -8 & =0 \\\\ 20\\theta  & =8 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{2}{5}.$"] ["question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf"] ["answer-f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa" :answer/id #uuid "f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa"] ["answer-f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}"] ["answer-d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8" :answer/id #uuid "d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8"] ["answer-d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["answer-4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786" :answer/id #uuid "4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786"] ["answer-4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786" :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer/id #uuid "694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a"] ["answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["answer-ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00" :answer/id #uuid "ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00"] ["answer-ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/correct "answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a"] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/choices "answer-f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa"] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/choices "answer-d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8"] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/choices "answer-4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786"] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/choices "answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a"] ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/choices "answer-ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00"] ["question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf"] [17592186162115 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c"] ["question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/id #uuid "b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1"] ["question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-159965"] ["question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=6\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?"] ["question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{2}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{2}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{2}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{6(\\theta -1)+2\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 6(\\theta -1)+2\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 8\\theta -6 & =0 \\\\ 8\\theta  & =6 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{3}{4}.$"] ["question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4"] ["answer-fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269" :answer/id #uuid "fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269"] ["answer-fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf" :answer/id #uuid "c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf"] ["answer-c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["answer-9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6" :answer/id #uuid "9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6"] ["answer-9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16" :answer/id #uuid "0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16"] ["answer-0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16" :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071" :answer/id #uuid "92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071"] ["answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/correct "answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071"] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/choices "answer-fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269"] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/choices "answer-c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf"] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/choices "answer-9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6"] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/choices "answer-0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16"] ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/choices "answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071"] ["question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4"] [17592186162115 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1"] ["question-a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" :question/id #uuid "a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad"] ["question-a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" :question/math-academy-id "q-159971"] ["question-a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Poisson random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-5\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?"] ["question-a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-5\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-5+\\frac{4}{\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5+\\frac{4}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-5\\theta +4}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ -5\\theta +4 & =0 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{4}{5}.$"] ["question-a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf"] ["answer-7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" :answer/id #uuid "7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7"] ["answer-7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" :answer/id #uuid "7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31"] ["answer-7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer/id #uuid "44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca"] ["answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["answer-dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" :answer/id #uuid "dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80"] ["answer-dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["answer-7bb1b0f3-0b13-5864-83a