d the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-4\\theta +8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡24) \\\\  & =-4+\\frac{8}{\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+\\frac{8}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-4\\theta +8}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ -4\\theta +8 & =0 \\\\ \\theta  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=2.$"] ["question-953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/id #uuid "332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467"] ["answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" :answer/id #uuid "4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01"] ["answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591" :answer/id #uuid "05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591"] ["answer-05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["answer-fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5" :answer/id #uuid "fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5"] ["answer-fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["answer-f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1" :answer/id #uuid "f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1"] ["answer-f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1" :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8" :answer/id #uuid "7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8"] ["answer-7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/correct "answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01"] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/choices "answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01"] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/choices "answer-05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591"] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/choices "answer-fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5"] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/choices "answer-f9cad329-3f44-5a46-8740-0f8924a257f1"] ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/choices "answer-7f9f706c-b703-5f30-8657-51f905019ad8"] ["question-953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467"] [17592186162115 :knowledge-point/questions "question-953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257"] ["question-d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" :question/id #uuid "d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161"] ["question-d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" :question/math-academy-id "q-159942"] ["question-d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent normal random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-3.54+2.2\\text{ }\\,\\theta -3\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-3.54+2.2\\text{ }\\,\\theta -3\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =2.2-6\\text{ }\\,\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.2-6\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 6\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =2.2 \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.367\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.367,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-5a1816a3-cd64-5456-9517-95ae4181b629" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1816a3-cd64-5456-9517-95ae4181b629"] ["answer-c15cc0bb-88d7-5a65-b0be-5fe61a791505" :answer/id #uuid "c15cc0bb-88d7-5a65-b0be-5fe61a791505"] ["answer-c15cc0bb-88d7-5a65-b0be-5fe61a791505" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c15cc0bb-88d7-5a65-b0be-5fe61a791505" :answer/value "0.065"] ["answer-e0b77137-f026-54f7-b0e8-585ac5b704af" :answer/id #uuid "e0b77137-f026-54f7-b0e8-585ac5b704af"] ["answer-e0b77137-f026-54f7-b0e8-585ac5b704af" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e0b77137-f026-54f7-b0e8-585ac5b704af" :answer/value "0.112"] ["answer-56d327c3-e05f-5754-88f5-dbc857c6043f" :answer/id #uuid "56d327c3-e05f-5754-88f5-dbc857c6043f"] ["answer-56d327c3-e05f-5754-88f5-dbc857c6043f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-56d327c3-e05f-5754-88f5-dbc857c6043f" :answer/value "0.204"] ["answer-12790bd2-fdb6-5ae2-9339-61f0fb556461" :answer/id #uuid "12790bd2-fdb6-5ae2-9339-61f0fb556