 the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-d69af2de-f48e-5047-98b1-6977b8b554d5" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -7.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\theta }-7.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\theta }-7.8 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\theta } & =7.8 \\\\ 4 & =7.8\\text{ }\\,\\theta  \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.513\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.513,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-d69af2de-f48e-5047-98b1-6977b8b554d5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f0558f9a-6e48-5095-9d94-0109cf7402ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0558f9a-6e48-5095-9d94-0109cf7402ad"] ["answer-da20a45a-b8d5-564b-b608-5e3791c34ad2" :answer/id #uuid "da20a45a-b8d5-564b-b608-5e3791c34ad2"] ["answer-da20a45a-b8d5-564b-b608-5e3791c34ad2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-da20a45a-b8d5-564b-b608-5e3791c34ad2" :answer/value "0.458"] ["answer-f91e9e3e-0341-5556-a0b5-5691bcc58340" :answer/id #uuid "f91e9e3e-0341-5556-a0b5-5691bcc58340"] ["answer-f91e9e3e-0341-5556-a0b5-5691bcc58340" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f91e9e3e-0341-5556-a0b5-5691bcc58340" :answer/value "0.513"] ["answer-67ea16bb-5fc8-5966-91a6-89f6143bb573" :answer/id #uuid "67ea16bb-5fc8-5966-91a6-89f6143bb573"] ["answer-67ea16bb-5fc8-5966-91a6-89f6143bb573" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-67ea16bb-5fc8-5966-91a6-89f6143bb573" :answer/value "0.617"] ["an