s\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-9.6+12.6\\text{ }\\,\\theta -8\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-54d12174-c052-5371-9f75-2200e071a1fb" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-9.6+12.6\\text{ }\\,\\theta -8\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =12.6-16\\text{ }\\,\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12.6-16\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 16\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =12.6 \\\\ \\theta  & ≈0.788\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}≈0.788,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-54d12174-c052-5371-9f75-2200e071a1fb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-0e02fd70-4bfa-5ee0-87ea-68ee321a3054" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e02fd70-4bfa-5ee0-87ea-68ee321a3054"] ["answer-c3d0c384-6c7e-5b36-a4e1-184863f1c6e7" :answer/id #uuid "c3d0c384-6c7e-5b36-a4e1-184863f1c6e7"] ["answer-c3d0c384-6c7e-5b36-a4e1-184863f1c6e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c3d0c384-6c7e-5b36-a4e1-184863f1c6e7" :answer/value "0.778"] ["answer-7ae6bb66-be05-5dcb-8863-b23c52551053" :answer/id #uuid "7ae6bb66-be05-5dcb-8863-b23c52551053"] ["answer-7ae6bb66-be05-5dcb-8863-b23c52551053" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7ae6bb66-be05-5dcb-8863-b23c52551053" :answer/value "0.788"] ["answer-f18f76ba-32bc-57a4-ac9a-52ff4682af02" :answer/id #uuid "f18f76ba-32bc-57a4-ac9a-52ff4682af02"] ["answer-f18f7